   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The Perfekt",
     "texto": [
      "To talk about what you did, the **Perfekt** is used, like the English present perfect: the present of **haben** + the **past participle**, which goes **at the end** of the sentence. **Ich habe einen Film gesehen** (I saw a movie; literally «I have a movie seen»).",
      "In speech, it covers both «I saw» and «I have seen»."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "How the past participle is formed",
     "texto": [
      "Regular verbs: **ge-** + stem + **-t**. machen → **gemacht**, kaufen → **gekauft**, spielen → **gespielt**. If the stem ends in -t: arbeiten → **gearbeitet**.",
      "Irregular verbs end in **-en** and sometimes change the vowel: essen → **gegessen**, sehen → **gesehen**, lesen → **gelesen**, trinken → **getrunken**.",
      "Verbs that begin with **be-** or **ver-** don't take «ge-»: besuchen → **besucht**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
